    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Graphic and type designer, Brooklyn-based, Czech-born (*1992). Trained in architecture (BA, Technical University of Liberec, 2016) then graphic design (MA, Academy of Arts Architecture and Design Prague, 2018). Work history: Henrik Nygren Design Stockholm (2016 placement), OK-RM London (2018-2019), independent studio Nedelka Bachor in Prague (2019-2022), Porto Rocha New York (2022, title: type designer). Founded Letter Books publishing imprint in 2019. Red Dot Best of Best 2020 for mmcite+ corporate identity. Approx 8-9 years experience since 2016. Mid-level to senior; specialist type/identity expertise. Autonomy 3 (set_by agent): has run independent work and published, but title and career arc suggest mid-level rather than creative-director autonomy. Work Status genuinely unclear: Porto Rocha about page (60+ names) does not list him as current team (checked 2026-06-17); partner Anezka Minarikova (Google Brand Studio, ex-Google Creative Lab 2022-2024) describes co-founding an independent design practice with Marek on her site, suggesting independent work alongside or after Porto Rocha; his own site lists Porto Rocha at 2022 with asterisk and no end date (page last updated Oct 2022, stale). LinkedIn snippet labels him type designer at Porto Rocha, likely cached/stale. Majority of external evidence points toward independent/studio status, but the asterisk may indicate ongoing. Jonathan confirmed currently employed in initial note, which conflicts with Porto Rocha team omission. Sources: mareknedelka.com/info, portorocha.com/about, anezkaminarikova.com, LinkedIn Google snippet, itsnicethat.com.",
